{
  "slug": "oracle-ai-data-platform-workbench-databricks-migrator",
  "name": "Oracle Ai Data Platform Workbench Databricks Migrator",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Drive the Oracle AI Data Platform (AIDP) Databricks Migration Toolkit in natural language. Plans and executes automated Databricks → AIDP migrations of notebooks, jobs, schedules, and catalog DDL — Pass-1 dependency rewrite + Pass-2 cell-by-cell execute/verify/fix on a live AIDP cluster with Claude.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **10 skills**, **2 agents** and **4 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (10): `aidp-acceptance-contract` (YAML-driven acceptance contract for batch and streaming pipelines that need convergence verification, not just \"no exceptions\"), `aidp-bucket-mapping` (Configure the s3:// → oci:// bucket / namespace mapping the migrator uses to rewrite paths during notebook +…), `aidp-build-dag` (Build a migration manifest (the execution DAG) from a Databricks workspace path or workflow ID), `aidp-check-data` (Pre-migration data-availability scan), `aidp-fixup-cell` (Targeted rewind of a migrated notebook), `aidp-migrate-catalog` (Migrate Databricks Unity Catalog / HMS schemas + tables onto AIDP), `aidp-migrate-job` (Run the full Databricks→AIDP migration against a manifest), `aidp-migrator-bootstrap` (One-shot environment readiness check for the Oracle AIDP Databricks migrator), and 2 more\n- **Agents** (2): `databricks-notebook-analyzer` (Use this agent when the user has pointed at a single Databricks notebook (.ipynb / .py / .scala)…), `migration-reviewer` (Use this agent after aidp-migrate-job completes to review a migrated .ipynb for correctness (NOT just \"did it run\"))\n- **Commands** (4): `check-data` (Pre-migration data-availability scan), `migrate-catalog` (Guided catalog migration flow), `migrate-job` (Guided full-job migration flow), `migration-status` (Parse + summarize the JOB_REPORT.md produced by a prior migration run)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install oracle-ai-data-platform-workbench-databricks-migrator@claude-plugins-official` from `oracle-samples/oracle-aidp-samples` (`ai/claude-code-plugins/oracle-ai-data-platform-workbench-databricks-migrator`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
